<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Babullah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1570">1570</a>–<a href="/years/1583">1583</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Sultan Babullah of Ternate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Babullah was sultan of Ternate in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maluku-islands">Maluku Islands</a> from 1570 to 1583. After the Portuguese murdered his father, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hairun">Hairun</a>, he besieged their fort on Ternate until they surrendered it in 1575, and extended the sultanate's influence over many islands of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>. In 1579 he received the English navigator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-drake">Francis Drake</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/babullah.jpg" alt="Babullah" width="294" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HHEHUM · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Babullah_1579_by_De_Bry.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
